<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.4.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00896</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.4.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>8762fd60-0a29-4b6d-8811-6319ee39c567</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> Match each equation with a verbal description that represents the same function.
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
      <item>\(f(x)=2x+4\) 
        
      </item>
    </list>
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> To get the output, multiply the input by 2, and then add 4 to the result.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>\(g(x)=2(x+4)\)</item>
    
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>To get the output, add 4 to the input, and then multiply the result by 2.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item>\(h(x)=4x+2\) 
      
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> To get the output, multiply the input by 4, and then add 2 to the result.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
    <item>\(k(x)=4(x+2)\) 
      
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>To get the output, add 2 to the input, and then multiply the result by 4.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Functions \(A\) and \(B\) are defined by these equations.
    \(A(x)=25+10x\)
    \(B(x)=80-15x\)
    Which function has a greater value when \(x\) is 2.5? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Function \(A\) has a greater value because \(B(2.5)=42.5\) and \(A(2.5)=50\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which function is greater when \(x = 4\)?</item>
</list>
<list>
     <item>\(f(x)=2x -7\)</item>
      <item>\(f(x) =-3x +1\)</item>
      <item>\(f(x)= -5x+2\)</item>
      <item>\(f(x)=x-10\)</item>
    </list>
  
<para><emphasis>Answer</emphasis><emphasis>:</emphasis> \(f(x)=2x -7\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which function rule describes the table below?
  </item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead/>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
       \(x\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
       2
      </entry>
      <entry>
       3
      </entry>
      <entry>
       4
      </entry>
      <entry>
       5
      </entry>
      <entry>
       6
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
       \(y\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
      3
      </entry>
      <entry>
        5
      </entry>
      <entry>
        7
      </entry>
      <entry>
       9
      </entry>
      <entry>
       11
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

  <list>
    <item>\(f(x)= x+1\)</item>
    <item>\(f(x) = 3x -3\)</item>
    <item>\(f(x)=2x-1\)</item>
    <item>\(f(x)= x+2\)</item>
  </list>
<para><emphasis>Answer</emphasis><emphasis>:</emphasis> \(f(x)=2x-1\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>Write a function \(g(x)\) for the following statement: To get the output, subtract 4 from the input, and then multiply the result by 2.
      </item>
</list>
    <list>
      <item>\(g(x)= 2x-4\)</item>
      <item>\(g(x)=-4 -2x\)</item>
      <item>\(g(x)=x -8\)</item>
      <item>\(g(x) = 2(x-4)\)</item>
    </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(g(x)=2(x-4)\)</para>
<para>6. Write a function \(h(x)\) for the following statement: To get the output, multiply the input by 5, and then add 2.</para>
<list>
  <item>\(h(x)= 5(x+2)\)</item>
  <item>\(h(x)=5x+2\)</item>
  <item>\(h(x)=x +2(5)\)</item>
  <item>\(h(x)= x+2\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(h(x)=5x+2\)</para>
<para>7. Find the value of \(f(x)= -2x -3\) when \(x =2\).</para>
<list>
  <item>7</item>
  <item>1</item>
  <item>–1</item>
  <item>–7</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer</emphasis><emphasis>:</emphasis> –7 </para>
<para>8. Write the rule from the table, and then find the value of \(g(2.5)\).</para>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
 <thead/>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
        \(x\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
      <entry>
       2
      </entry>
      <entry>
       3
      </entry>
      <entry>
        4
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
       \(g(x)\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
      2
      </entry>
      <entry>
       6
      </entry>
      <entry>
      10
      </entry>
      <entry>
      14
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(g(x)=4x-2\), \(g(2.5)=8\)</para></section>
</content>
